# TypeScript Style Conventions

## Arrow Functions

Always use arrow functions. Never use the `function` keyword for declarations.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
export function fetchData(id: string) { ... }
function handleClick() { ... }

// ✅ GOOD
export const fetchData = (id: string) => { ... }
const handleClick = () => { ... }
```

## No Single-Letter Variable Names

Variables must have descriptive names, even in short scopes.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
const d = dayjs(date)
arr.map((e) => e.id)
const [v, setV] = useState(0)

// ✅ GOOD
const parsed = dayjs(date)
arr.map((entry) => entry.id)
const [count, setCount] = useState(0)
```
